1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,580
EWMA has one knob, and everything follows from it.

2
00:00:04,666 --> 00:00:06,633
Each new point blends the fresh

3
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:09,366
reading with everything that came before.

4
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:13,734
Unroll that recursion and the weights fall away geometrically.

5
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:16,835
At lambda zero point two, each step back

6
00:00:16,935 --> 00:00:20,093
weighs eighty percent of the one in front.

7
00:00:20,783 --> 00:00:23,275
That memory changes the limits.

8
00:00:23,366 --> 00:00:26,554
Plot the limit width against the subgroup number.

9
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:31,038
A Shewhart chart holds the same three sigma limits throughout.

10
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:35,620
The EWMA limits start wide, because early on there is

11
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:41,593
little accumulated evidence, then tighten as weighted history builds.

12
00:00:41,683 --> 00:00:44,391
They close on an asymptote near one

13
00:00:44,491 --> 00:00:47,199
sigma, a band three times narrower.

14
00:00:47,283 --> 00:00:50,044
Tighter limits on smoothed data catch a

15
00:00:50,144 --> 00:00:52,391
slow drift about twice as early.

16
00:00:52,483 --> 00:00:56,055
Lambda sets how much of the past the chart keeps.

